  "verbalization": "Junceelloside C is consistently linked to GR-ST through multiple pathways, all involving Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta as a key intermediate. The evidence suggests that junceelloside C acts as a target for several compounds, including [(18E)-11-chloro-21-hydroxy-12,20-dimethoxy-2,5,9,16-tetramethyl-8,23-dioxo-4,24-dioxa-9,22-diazatetracyclo[19.3.1.110,14.03,5]hexacosa-10,12,14(26),16,18-pentaen-6-yl] 2-[methyl(2-methylpropanoyl)amino]propanoate, (3S,8S,9S,10R,13S,14S,16S)-17-[(1S)-1-(1,5-dimethylpiperidin-2-yl)ethyl]-10,13-dimethyl-2,3,4,7,8,9,11,12,14,15,16,17-dodecahydro-1H-cyclopenta[a]phenanthrene-3,16-diol, and methyl oleanolate. These compounds all target the same enzyme, indicating a potential mechanism of action through this enzyme. The consistent targeting of Sn1-specific diacylglycerol lipase beta by junceelloside C suggests that it may modulate lipid metabolism, which is a plausible pathway for its interaction with GR-ST. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between junceelloside C and GR-ST through the regulation of this enzyme, though the exact biological role of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
